WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.200
"Why the IQs of Vegetarian
Children Are Higher"

00:00:06.352 --> 00:00:07.880
Many vegetarian parents believe

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.960
their children are brighter
than omnivorous kids,

00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:14.520
but you don't really know
until you put it to the test.

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:16.960
And, indeed,
the IQ of vegetarian children

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:20.240
tested about 16 points
higher than average,

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.960
and their mental age exceeded
their chronological age

00:00:22.960 --> 00:00:24.560
by about a year.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.240
The researchers knew
the veg kids were bright,

00:00:27.240 --> 00:00:29.960
but why were they
so much more superior?

00:00:30.520 --> 00:00:32.360
There are obviously
confounding factors,

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:34.480
like maybe more highly
educated parents

00:00:34.480 --> 00:00:36.800
are more likely to have
vegetarian children,

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.240
and they pass down both
their brains and their diets.

00:00:40.240 --> 00:00:42.720
Even if there is
a cause-and-effect relationship

00:00:42.720 --> 00:00:45.040
between vegetarianism and IQ,

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:48.240
were the children smarter
because they were vegetarians,

00:00:48.240 --> 00:00:51.640
or did they become vegetarian
because they were so smart?

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:55.240
Researchers in the UK followed
8,000 kids for decades.

00:00:55.240 --> 00:00:57.440
They measured their IQ
at age 10,

00:00:57.440 --> 00:00:59.000
then came back 20 years later

00:00:59.000 --> 00:01:02.960
and asked which of them had
become vegetarian during that time.

00:01:02.960 --> 00:01:05.440
And, indeed, the smarter kids
had an increased likelihood

00:01:05.440 --> 00:01:08.080
of being a vegetarian
as an adult.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.440
The researchers even quoted
Benjamin Franklin,

00:01:10.440 --> 00:01:13.120
saying that vegetarian
diets result in

00:01:13.120 --> 00:01:16.560
"Greater clearness of head
and quicker comprehension."

00:01:16.560 --> 00:01:18.920
According to the largest
and oldest association

00:01:18.920 --> 00:01:21.200
of nutrition professionals
in the world,

00:01:21.200 --> 00:01:23.160
strictly plant-based
diets are appropriate

00:01:23.160 --> 00:01:25.360
for all stages of
the life cycle,

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:26.920
including childhood,

00:01:26.920 --> 00:01:29.640
and may indeed
provide health benefits.

00:01:29.640 --> 00:01:32.800
What about plant-based diets
and growth in children?

00:01:32.800 --> 00:01:34.200
Some studies show that children

00:01:34.200 --> 00:01:36.600
raised on restrictive
macrobiotic diets

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:38.560
suffer from growth stunting,

00:01:38.560 --> 00:01:41.040
while others show
that those raised plant-based

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.080
may end up being
up to an inch (2.5 cm) taller.

00:01:44.080 --> 00:01:45.920
In a systematic review
and meta-analysis

00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:49.160
of children on vegan diets,
heights were lower in vegans,

00:01:49.160 --> 00:01:51.320
but only because
they included a study

00:01:51.320 --> 00:01:54.720
in which the vegan kids
were significantly younger,

00:01:54.720 --> 00:01:57.040
mostly 10 to 14 years old,

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.840
compared to mostly
15 to 19 years old.

00:02:00.840 --> 00:02:03.720
Once you remove the study
with the age disparity,

00:02:03.720 --> 00:02:06.800
the height disparity
also disappears.

00:02:06.800 --> 00:02:08.840
What about width disparity?

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:11.240
Population studies indicate
that vegetarian diets

00:02:11.240 --> 00:02:14.120
are associated with
a lower prevalence of obesity

00:02:14.120 --> 00:02:16.750
in both adults and children.

